CDSD \citep{brouillard_causal_2024} aims to recover both the latent variables and the temporal causal graph over these latents from a high-dimensional time series, where the causal graph is shown to be identifiable under the strong \emph{single-parent decoding assumption} -- i.e. each observed variable is mapped to a single latent, while each latent can be the parent of multiple observed variables. This assumption is well-suited to modeling long-range climate dynamics and teleconnections, where variations in distinct regions around the world can causally affect the climate in other regions. 
