    \caption{Tunneling durations \tauB (green crosses) in experimental strong field ionization of Ar as a function of the laser intensity. The durations were extracted out of the widths of the PMDs published in Ref.~\cite{Arissian2010} using Eq.~\ref{eq:distribution_p}. The green shaded area corresponds to the published statistical error on the PMD width.
    The experimental data are compared to various theoretical results: numerical solutions of  Eq.~\eqref{eq:gamma_phi} (solid line); adiabatic limit (dashed line); data extracted from the resolution of the TDSE on a model Ar atom (empty squares).  The triangle indicates the value obtained out of the TDSE PMDs averaged over an experimentally realistic intensity  distribution centered at $\IL{=}0.18 \; \rm PW \ cm^{-2}$.} 
    \label{fig:Arissian}
