      \field{abstract}{We generalize the Demailly approximation theorem from complex geometry to Arakelov geometry. As an application, let X/Q be an integral projective variety and N‾ be an adelic line bundle on X. We prove that ess(N‾)≥0 ⟹ N‾ pseudo-effective. This was proved in [1], assuming N‾ relatively semipositive. We show in the appendix that the above assertion is also true for adelic line bundles on quasi-projective varieties, under the framework of [17].}
