      \field{labelnamesource}{author}
      \field{labeltitlesource}{title}
      \field{abstract}{We use the differentiability of the arithmetic volume function and an arithmetic Bertini type theorem to classify when one can find a closed point on the generic fiber of an arithmetic variety, whose heights with respect to some finite tuple of arithmetic \$\textbackslash mathbb\{R\}\$-divisors approximate a given tuple of real numbers. We use this result to prove existential closedness of \$\textbackslash overline\{\textbackslash mathbb\{Q\}\}\$ as a globally valued field (abbreviated GVF). We introduce GVF functionals on the space of arithmetic \$\textbackslash mathbb\{R\}\$-divisors and interpret the essential infimum function as the infimum of values of normalised GVF functionals, at least when the generic part of the arithmetic \$\textbackslash mathbb\{R\}\$-divisor is big. We also give a new criterion on equality in one of the Zhang's inequalities.}
