Quantitatively, the crossover from weak to moderate rotation ($\omega \simeq 0.5$-$3$) produces shifts of a few~eV--well within the resolution of optical and magneto-transport probes in semiconductor quantum rings.  
In the strong-rotation domain ($\omega \gtrsim 5$) the near-degeneracy of different $n$ manifolds, together with the persistent splitting among $m$ branches, is expected to enhance the amplitude of persistent currents through inter-level mixing.  
