\subsubsection{EL switch time and model efficiency analysis}
A commonly emphasized objective in existing studies is the reduction of treatment delivery time \cite{wuyckens2025proton, qian2023novel, liu2020novel, ma2024machine, zhang2022energy}. The duration of arc delivery is influenced by various machine-specific factors, such as the number and order of ELs, spot positions, and gantry angles. Among these, ELS time often contributes the most to overall delivery time, especially when the number of energy layers and energy switch-ups is not minimized \cite{wuyckens2025proton, qian2023novel, liu2020novel}. The ELS time is evaluated and analyzed for both SPArc\textsubscript{ps} and SPArc\textsubscript{dl}. The efficiency to generate EL pre-selection, or the inference time of SPArc\textsubscript{dl}, is also reported. 

