In contrast, we highlight the underexplored setting where (H)LV is inherent and may carry an informative signal, arguing that its integration into the AL framework requires rethinking core components such as acquisition and annotation strategies.

\paragraph{Relabeling}
Relabeling, i.e., collecting additional annotations for previously labeled instances to reduce noise or correct errors, is explored in \citet{chen-yu-and-samuel-r-bowman-2022-clean, goh2023ActiveLabActiveLearning, lin2016ReActiveLearningActive}. These approaches implicitly challenge assumptions \textbf{A2} and \textbf{A3} by acknowledging annotation errors and varying difficulty. However, they treat disagreement as an error rather than a potentially meaningful signal. 

\paragraph{HLV-aware AL}
