\section{Conclusion}

In this work, we build upon the BEST-RQ paradigm to create a new generation of open-source SSL music audio representation models for music. These models can be applied to various music analysis tasks, and we envision their usage by music information retrieval researchers and practitioners and beyond. We expect them to foster further advancements in representation learning research and downstream music audio analysis tasks, with potential for developing final applications.
To develop our models, we experimented with SOTA SSL methodologies based on masked token prediction to build models with a higher overall performance across a range of benchmark music audio analysis tasks.
Our technical contributions include experimental results utilizing parallel codebooks, multi-feature targets, and other quantization strategies. 

