\section{DISCUSSION AND FUTURE WORKS}
% We explore the idea of physics informed reinforcement learning, with the aim to improve the control of dynamical legged robots with arms. This work developed a unified RL framework to efficiently learn the whole-body control of a quadruped with an arm, by integrating the explicit kinematics model within the RL framework as an effective way to inform physics based information in the form of kinematics, which is promising for future extensions. This indicates that in long-term, our research community can explore more explicit and rich physics model-based information into learning structures, and regularize the neural network's output to adhere to physics laws. The future work will focus on the extension of physics formed learning, which will enable more sophisticated high-level planner that will be capable of planning the navigation on complex environments, while the whole-body control autonomously guarantees the smooth coordination between the body and the arm for executing a wide range of real-world operations. 
We develop a unified RL framework that integrates explicit kinematics models, enabling efficient whole-body skills of a quadruped with a manipulator, which effectively incorporates physics-based information in the form of kinematics and is promising for future extensions. Future work will extend physics-informed learning and integrate more detailed physics models into learning structures, ensuring neural network outputs adhere to physical laws. This new capability will autonomously produce highly dynamic and coherent whole-body motor skills, and allow us to develop more sophisticated high-level planners to navigate complex environments for a wide range of real-world operations. 

