\subsection{Addressing Counterarguments}

\subsubsection{Reductionism Critique}
Some worry that labeling simple devices (thermostats) as “observers” trivializes the concept. We rebut that minimal observers are foundational building blocks: layering, second-order loops, or enriched predictive mechanisms $h$ can yield the complexity of conscious or social systems. The presence of feedback and boundary definition $\mathcal{B}$ is the \emph{sine qua non} of observation, whether in a simple or advanced entity.

\subsubsection{Infinite Regress in Self-Reference}
Second-order or multi-layer observers can appear to regress infinitely: who observes the observer’s observer, etc.? We propose hierarchical encapsulation: each observer only references or modifies a finite subset of its own states. Formally, we forbid cycles of observation that do not converge or yield stable references. This ensures a well-founded partial order in the lattice of meta-observation relations.

